        </li>
        <li class="card reveal">
          <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="8" cy="15" r="4"/><path d="m11 12 9-9M17 6l3 3M14 9l2 2"/></svg></div>
          <div><strong>Requests for passwords, MFA codes or card details.</strong> <span>Nobody legitimate needs your MFA code.</span></div>
        </li>
        <li class="card reveal">
          <div class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="6" y="2" width="12" height="20" rx="2"/><path d="M12 6v7M9 10l3 3 3-3M10 18h4"/></svg></div>
          <div><strong>Prompts to install an app</strong> <span>or approve a sign-in you didn't start.</span></div>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <a class="next reveal" href="#before">Next <svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M6 13l6 6 6-6"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== 04 Before you scan ===== -->
  <section class="panel" id="before" aria-labelledby="before-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="kicker reveal" aria-hidden="true">04 / 06</div>
      <h2 id="before-h" class="reveal">Before you scan</h2>
      <ul class="checks" role="list" data-stagger>
        <li class="card reveal"><div class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-10"/></svg></div>Ask yourself who put the code there and whether you can verify it.</li>
        <li class="card reveal"><div class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-10"/></svg></div>Read the link preview your phone shows before you tap to open it.</li>
        <li class="card reveal"><div class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-10"/></svg></div>If it claims to be a company system, go to it the way you normally would instead of using the code.</li>
        <li class="card reveal"><div class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="m5 12 5 5 9-10"/></svg></div>Not sure? Don't scan. Ask the Information Security team.</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="next reveal" href="#entered">Next <svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M6 13l6 6 6-6"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== 05 If you entered your details ===== -->
  <section class="panel urgent" id="entered" aria-labelledby="entered-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="kicker red reveal" aria-hidden="true">05 / 06</div>
      <h2 id="entered-h" class="reveal">If you entered your details on a suspicious page</h2>
      <p class="alert reveal">Act straight away. Speed matters far more than blame, and you will not be in trouble for reporting.</p>
      <ol class="steps" role="list" data-stagger>
        <li class="reveal"><strong>Change your password now</strong> from a trusted device, by going directly to the real site (not through the QR code or any link you were sent).</li>
        <li class="reveal"><strong>Report it immediately</strong> to Information Security using the button below.</li>
        <li class="reveal"><strong>Tell us if you approved an MFA prompt</strong> or shared a code, so sessions can be revoked.</li>
        <li class="reveal"><strong>Changed the same password elsewhere?</strong> If you reuse it on other accounts, change those too.</li>
        <li class="reveal"><strong>Keep the evidence.</strong> Don't delete the email or text. Take a photo of the poster or sticker and note where you saw it.</li>
        <li class="reveal"><strong>Entered card or bank details?</strong> Contact your bank straight away.</li>
      </ol>
      <a class="next reveal" href="#report">Next <svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M6 13l6 6 6-6"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== 06 Report it ===== -->
  <section class="panel" id="report" aria-labelledby="report-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="kicker reveal" aria-hidden="true">06 / 06</div>
      <div class="card report reveal">
        <h2 id="report-h">Report it</h2>
        <p class="text">Report a suspicious QR code, or any concern that your account or data may have been compromised, even if you're not certain:</p>
        <p class="email">information.security@macedragados.com</p>
        <p class="text">Include what you scanned, where and when you saw it, and what (if anything) you entered.</p>
        <a class="btn" href="mailto:information.security@macedragados.com?subject=Suspected%20QR%20code%20phishing%20report">
          <svg class="i" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 2 11 13M22 2l-7 20-4-9-9-4 20-7z"/></svg>
          Email Information Security
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

<footer>
  MDJV Information Security team &middot; Security awareness campaign &middot; If in doubt, report it.
</footer>

<script>
(function () {
  'use strict';
  var root = document.documentElement;
  root.classList.add('js');
  var reduceMotion = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
  var each = function (list, fn) { Array.prototype.forEach.call(list, fn); };

  // Scroll reveal, staggered within groups.
  var items = document.querySelectorAll('.reveal');
  if ('IntersectionObserver' in window && !reduceMotion) {
    each(document.querySelectorAll('[data-stagger]'), function (group) {
      each(group.querySelectorAll('.reveal'), function (el, i) { el.style.transitionDelay = Math.min(i * 80, 480) + 'ms'; });
    });
    var revealer = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
      entries.forEach(function (e) {
        if (e.isIntersecting) { e.target.classList.add('in'); revealer.unobserve(e.target); }
      });
    }, { threshold: 0.05, rootMargin: '0px 0px -6% 0px' });
    each(items, function (el) { revealer.observe(el); });
  } else {
    each(items, function (el) { el.classList.add('in'); });
  }

  // Reading progress bar.
  var bar = document.querySelector('.progress');
  var ticking = false;
  var updateBar = function () {
    var max = root.scrollHeight - window.innerHeight;
    var p = max > 0 ? Math.min(1, Math.max(0, window.scrollY / max)) : 0;
    bar.style.transform = 'scaleX(' + p + ')';
    ticking = false;
  };
  var onScroll = function () { if (!ticking) { ticking = true; window.requestAnimationFrame(updateBar); } };
  window.addEventListener('scroll', onScroll, { passive: true });
  window.addEventListener('resize', onScroll, { passive: true });
  updateBar();

  // Highlight the current section in the side dots (desktop).
  if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) {
    var dots = {};
    each(document.querySelectorAll('.dots a'), function (a) { dots[a.getAttribute('href').slice(1)] = a; });
    var spy = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
      entries.forEach(function (e) {
        if (!e.isIntersecting || !dots[e.target.id]) return;
        Object.keys(dots).forEach(function (k) { dots[k].removeAttribute('aria-current'); });
        dots[e.target.id].setAttribute('aria-current', 'true');
      });
    }, { rootMargin: '-45% 0px -50% 0px' });
    Object.keys(dots).forEach(function (id) { var s = document.getElementById(id); if (s) spy.observe(s); });
  }
  // Anonymous visit count (GoatCounter: no cookies, no personal data).
  // An optional ?src=<tag> on the QR link is recorded so scans can be split by poster location.
  try {
    var host = location.hostname;
    if (location.protocol !== 'file:' && host !== 'localhost' && host !== '127.0.0.1') {
      var tag = (new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('src') || '').toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9-]/g, '').slice(0, 40);
      var path = location.pathname + (tag ? '?src=' + tag : '');
      new Image().src = 'https://mdjvinformationsecurity.goatcounter.com/count?p=' + encodeURIComponent(path) +
        '&t=' + encodeURIComponent(document.title) + '&rnd=' + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2);
    }
  } catch (e) { /* counting must never break the page */ }
})();
</script>
